{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1025655-armor-conversion-question-for-cofd-and-a-specific-one-about-dragon-skin","id":1025655,"title":"Armor conversion question for CofD (and a specific one about Dragon Skin)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-02T18:14:05-08:00","id":1025655,"title":"Armor conversion question for CofD (and a specific one about Dragon Skin)","content":"Hello all. My apologies if this has been asked...I did try to search it up before posting.<br /> <br /> I was comparing the two tables of armor - the one in the nWod core book (p. 170) and the armor table from CofD (p. 270). It seems like the developers added one more point of protection to the ballistic side. Maybe it's (painfully) obvious, but doesn't this lessen the effect of changing firearms to have automatic successes?<br /> <br /> Anyway, my question is about converting armor from nWod sources to CofD. Would one simply, as mentioned, add a point to ballistic armor protection and call it done? It seems like everything else is the same (more or less) in the other columns.<br /> <br /> I also have a specific question about Dragon Skin armor, from Armory Reloaded (pg. 142). Would this armor be converted the above way? I'm not quite sure how to convert it true to CofD. According to the book, all ballistic damage taken is reduced to bashing, then reduced by one (before applying the protection value of the armor). Converting all ballistic to bashing (and reducing it by one) in CofD would be very powerful. How would you all convert it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12124-lord-dynel","name":"Lord Dynel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T03:54:59-08:00","id":1026439,"title":"","content":"Well, I took a stab at converting it myself though I had hoped on getting some feedback from those more experienced. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, I made the armor 2/5 (keeping in line with other armor conversions), and kept the same stats otherwise (Strength 1, Defense 0, Speed 0, and Cost/Availability \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf). I also kept the feature that it removes a point of ballistic damage (before the effects of armor are applied). It seems fairly powerful, but for the cost I think it's fair. I'm running a low-level super/vigilante game and my both of my players are realizing the importance of such things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12124-lord-dynel","name":"Lord Dynel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}